.email-meta .row .key { color: var(--color-text-muted); min-width: 64px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; padding-top: 0.15rem; }
.email-meta .row .val { color: var(--color-text); word-break: break-word; }
.email-meta .row .val.subject { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 600; }
.email-stage { display: inline-block; background: #1e40af; color: #ffffff; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
.email-stage.posted { background: #1e40af; color: #ffffff; }
.email-stage.submitted { background: #92400e; color: #ffffff; }
.email-stage.merged { background: #065f46; color: #ffffff; }
.email-stage.paid { background: #047857; color: #ffffff; }
.email-body { padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem; color: var(--color-text); line-height: 1.6; font-size: 0.95rem; }
.email-body h2 { color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
.email-body p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
.email-body .data-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
.email-body .data-table th, .email-body .data-table td { text-align: left; padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); font-size: 0.88rem; }
.email-body .data-table th { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-weight: 500; width: 40%; }
.email-body .data-table td { color: var(--color-text); font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; word-break: break-word; }
.email-body .btn-link { display: inline-block; background: #1e40af; color: #ffffff; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; margin: 0.25rem 0; }
.email-body .btn-link:hover { background: #1d4ed8; color: #ffffff; }
.email-body code { background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-surface), var(--color-text) 8%); color: var(--color-text); padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
.email-body .footer-note { margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 0.85rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; }
.email-body a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; }
.email-body a:hover { color: var(--color-primary-dark); }
.email-body .footer-note a { text-decoration: underline; }
p a, ol a, ul a, li a, .intro a { text-decoration: underline; }
.intro { background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary); padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
.intro strong { color: var(--color-text); }
.intro code { background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-surface), var(--color-text) 8%); color: var(--color-text); padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.88rem; }
</style>
<h1>Confirmation Emails Sent to Clients</h1>
<p>Every paid PrTask transaction triggers four confirmation emails to the cardholder's verified email address. Each email is timestamped, references the task ID and (where applicable) the Maya transaction reference, and links back to the on-platform record. Together these emails form the digital equivalent of an acknowledgment / delivery receipt trail. The four emails below are the production templates rendered with the same example transaction (PR cli/cli#1) used in the <a href="/Receipt?pr=https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/1">delivery receipt page</a>.</p>
<div class="intro"><strong>Note for Maya Business reviewers:</strong> The email content below is the actual production template. In a live transaction every <code>{placeholder}</code> is replaced with the corresponding TaskEntity, PullRequestEntity, PaymentEntity, and UserEntity field from the platform database. Sender domain is <code>prtask.com</code> via SendGrid, with SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records published.</div>
