<section class="page-description">
    <h2>How these emails fit into the delivery proof</h2>
    <p>The four emails above arrive in the cardholder's verified inbox over the lifetime of a single PrTask transaction. Together with the merged pull request on GitHub and the corresponding entry in the <a href="/SystemLogs">system event log</a>, they form a complete, independently verifiable record that the digital service was delivered, accepted by the cardholder, and paid for. The Stage 3 email is the canonical delivery acknowledgment because it documents the cardholder's explicit accept-and-merge action; the Stage 4 email is the paid receipt linking that delivery to the Maya Business transaction reference.</p>
</section>
